---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Icon from "../components/Icon.astro";
import { site, ext } from "../data/site";
---
<Base title="Download" description="Download Saya for Windows. Linux builds are on the way.">
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 pt-20">
    <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl">Download Saya</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-xl text-lg text-paper/70">Every release is listed on GitHub together with its checksum.</p>
    <ul class="mt-12 divide-y divide-white/10 border-y border-white/10">
      <li class="flex flex-col gap-4 py-8 sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between">
        <div><h2 class="text-2xl">Windows</h2><p class="mt-1 text-paper/60">Windows 10 or later, 64-bit. Version {site.version}.</p></div>
        <a href={site.releaseUrl} class="btn bg-accent text-ink" {...ext(site.releaseUrl)}><Icon name="download" class="size-5" />Download</a>
      </li>
      <li class="flex flex-col gap-4 py-8 sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between">
        <div><h2 class="text-2xl">Linux</h2><p class="mt-1 text-paper/60">AppImage and .deb packages are coming soon.</p></div>
        <span class="btn cursor-not-allowed bg-white/10 text-paper/50" aria-disabled="true">Coming soon</span>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <h2 class="mt-20 text-2xl">Verify your download</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-lg text-paper/70">Compare the SHA-256 checksum in the release notes with the one for your file. In PowerShell:</p>
    <pre class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl bg-white/[0.06] p-5"><code>Get-FileHash .\YOUR-FILE -Algorithm SHA256</code></pre>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-paper/60">The alpha build isn't code-signed yet, so Windows SmartScreen may show a warning. Only choose "Run anyway" if the checksums match.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
